1
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:14,620
A driving app estimates braking distance in metres with the expression v squared over 20, plus v over 3.

2
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:18,250
Here v is the speed in kilometres per hour.

3
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,880
Engineers test it with different values of v.

4
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:24,130
What is its value when v is 30?

5
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:27,850
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:32,150
30 squared is 900, and 900 over 20 is 45.

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,830
30 over 3 is 10.

8
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:40,460
So the braking distance is 45 plus 10, which is 55 metres.

9
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:47,920
If someone types negative 30 by mistake, v squared is still 900, but v over 3 is negative 10.

10
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:51,600
The app gives 35, which makes no sense.

11
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:59,410
Remember the order of operations: brackets, then indices, then multiply and divide, then add and subtract.

12
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:02,530
Replace each letter by its value in brackets.

13
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,570
Then follow the order of operations.

14
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:08,170
Take care when a value is negative.

15
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:14,540
When A is negative 3, negative A squared is negative 9, because only the 3 is squared.

16
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:17,090
And A cubed is negative 27.

17
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:17,800
Your turn.

18
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:20,060
What is negative 3, all squared?

19
00:01:20,110 --> 00:01:23,370
Pause the video and try it.

20
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:26,450
Negative 3 times negative 3 is positive 9.

21
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:30,290
A negative number squared is always positive.

22
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:34,810
A counter-example is one case that shows a statement is false.

23
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:37,280
N squared is always bigger than N?

24
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:40,890
No: when N is 0.5, N squared is only 0.25.

25
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:42,220
Here is the method.

26
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:48,400
Step 1: write the expression, with each letter replaced by its value in brackets.

27
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:50,840
Step 2: work out the powers first.

28
00:01:50,890 --> 00:01:53,550
Take care with negative signs.

29
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:58,060
Step 3: then multiply and divide, then add and subtract.

30
00:01:58,110 --> 00:02:01,890
Step 4: ask yourself: is the answer sensible?

31
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:07,440
Find 3 X squared, minus 2 Y cubed, when X is negative 4 and Y is 2.

32
00:02:07,490 --> 00:02:13,180
3 times negative 4, all squared, is 3 times 16, which is 48.

33
00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:17,190
2 times 2 cubed is 2 times 8, which is 16.

34
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:19,460
48 minus 16 is 32.

35
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:20,160
Your turn.

36
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:22,730
What is X cubed when X is negative 2?

37
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:25,670
Pause and work it out.

38
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,320
Negative 2 times negative 2 is 4.

39
00:02:28,370 --> 00:02:30,980
4 times negative 2 is negative 8.

40
00:02:31,030 --> 00:02:34,670
A negative number cubed stays negative.

41
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:39,460
Find P plus Q, over P minus Q, when P is 7 and Q is negative 3.

42
00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:42,580
The top is 7 plus negative 3, which is 4.

43
00:02:42,630 --> 00:02:46,630
The bottom is 7 minus negative 3, which is 10.

44
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:49,200
4 over 10 is 0.4.

45
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:52,380
Ella finds 2 X squared when X is negative 5.

46
00:02:52,430 --> 00:02:54,380
Which line is wrong?

47
00:02:54,430 --> 00:02:55,530
Line 1 is wrong.

48
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:57,840
Indices come before multiplying.

49
00:02:57,890 --> 00:03:00,410
Square the negative 5 first.

50
00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:05,620
Negative 5 squared is 25, and 2 times 25 is 50.

51
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:11,710
Spreadsheets and apps substitute values into formulae millions of times a day.

52
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:19,160
Engineers test them with negative, zero and huge inputs, to make sure the answers are always sensible.

53
00:03:19,210 --> 00:03:20,330
One last question.

54
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,930
What is negative X squared, when X is 4?

55
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:26,080
Pause the video and answer.

56
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:27,510
Only X is squared.

57
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:32,830
4 squared is 16, and the negative sign makes it negative 16.

58
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:36,450
To remember: substitute values in brackets.

59
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,140
A negative number squared is positive.

60
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:41,240
Cubed, it is negative.

61
00:03:41,290 --> 00:03:46,990
Indices come before multiplying and dividing, then adding and subtracting.

62
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:50,940
One counter-example proves a statement is false.

63
00:03:50,990 --> 00:03:56,110
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.1 on Camday.
